{
  "name": "Mote of Potential",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "YCWsDK3A3zP6UqYf",
  "img": "icons/magic/symbols/star-yellow.webp",
  "folder": "DAG7Y53qWjX6OzXK",
  "sort": 100000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Whenever you give a creature a Bardic Inspiration die, you can utter a note from the Song of Creation to create a Tiny mote of potential, which orbits within 5 feet of that creature. The mote is intangible and invulnerable, lasts until the Bardic Inspiration die is lost, and looks like a musical note, a star, a flower, or another symbol of art or life that you choose. When the creature uses the die, the mote adds an effect depending on the roll.</p><p><strong>Ability Check.</strong> When the creature rolls the Bardic Inspiration die for an ability check, it can roll the die again and choose which roll to use, as the mote pops in colorful, harmless sparks.</p><p><strong>Attack Roll.</strong> Immediately after the creature rolls the die for an attack roll against a target, the mote shatters thunderously. The target and each creature of your choice you can see within 5 feet of it must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or take Thunder damage equal to the number rolled on the die.</p><p><strong>Saving Throw.</strong> Immediately after the creature rolls the die for a saving throw, the mote vanishes with the sound of soft music, and the creature gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the number rolled plus your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1).</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-dwlU9IdeYUsiBQ0J\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The Thunder damage equals the number rolled on the die: replace the rolled formula by that number if needed.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
